! name: Daily Driver
! description: General-purpose search. Discards the worst everyday spam (listicle/SEO farms, fake fix sites), downranks lesser offenders, and boosts trustworthy troubleshooting/reference/review sources.
! public: false
! author: Mark

! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Philosophy: not a narrow topic Goggle -- meant to be the default driver for
! everyday search. Uses the full toolkit (discard/downrank/boost) rather than
! staying downrank-only: the worst repeat-offender domains are discarded
! outright, weaker offenders are downranked, and a handful of consistently
! good sources (real forums, hands-on reviews, reference sites) get boosted
! so they surface ahead of SEO noise without needing a closed/allowlist
! Goggle. No leading generic $discard, so recall stays open for everything
! not explicitly listed here.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

! =====================================
! 1. DISCARD -- worst everyday offenders
! =====================================
! Fake tech-fix sites, image-loop/clickbait content, AI-generated listicles,
! and scraped SO/GitHub mirrors that add nothing over the original source.
$discard,site=pinterest.com
$discard,site=quora.com
$discard,site=ehow.com
$discard,site=wikihow.com
$discard,site=screenrant.com
$discard,site=cbr.com
$discard,site=softonic.com
$discard,site=fandom.com
$discard,site=cnet.com

! Scraped Stack Overflow / GitHub mirrors (see tech-research.goggle for the
! more thorough technical-search version of this list)
$discard,site=itectec.com
$discard,site=qastack.com

! =====================================
! 2. DOWNRANK -- lesser SEO/content-farm/tutorial-mill offenders
! =====================================
! Not bad enough to discard outright, but reliably lower-quality than
! competing results for the same query.
$downrank=1,site=answers.com
$downrank=2,site=geeksforgeeks.org
$downrank=1,site=w3schools.com

! =====================================
! 3. BOOST -- troubleshooting heroes
! =====================================
! For "how to fix..." queries: forces real humans and actual forums/repos to
! the top instead of fake blogs.
$boost=8,site=reddit.com
$boost=8,site=stackoverflow.com
$boost=8,site=stackexchange.com
$boost=7,site=github.com
$boost=7,site=ifixit.com

! =====================================
! 4. BOOST -- trusted reviews & tech
! =====================================
! For shopping/gear research: boosts sites that do real, physical testing
! over affiliate-link spammers.
$boost=6,site=rtings.com
$boost=5,site=gsmarena.com
$boost=5,site=theverge.com

! =====================================
! 5. BOOST -- everyday reference
! =====================================
! Keeps standard, quick-reference sites highly visible.
$boost=6,site=wikipedia.org
$boost=5,site=imdb.com
$boost=5,site=goodreads.com

! =====================================
! 6. BOOST -- news (wire-service / major outlets)
! =====================================
! Established outlets with actual reporting, favored over aggregators and
! SEO-optimized "news" rewrite sites.
$boost=6,site=cbc.ca
$boost=6,site=bbc.com
$boost=6,site=nytimes.com
$boost=6,site=aljazeera.com

! Canadian & international editorial/opinion outlets
$boost=5,site=theglobeandmail.com
$boost=5,site=macleans.ca
$boost=5,site=thewalrus.ca
$boost=5,site=thetyee.ca
$boost=5,site=thestar.com
$boost=5,site=economist.com

! =====================================
! 7. BOOST -- canada: government & official sources
! =====================================
! For queries about benefits, taxes, immigration, statistics, law, etc.
! Starting with federal sources; add provincial ones (ontario.ca,
! gov.bc.ca, alberta.ca, quebec.ca, ...) as needed.
!
! Note: `site=gc.ca` is included as a catch-all since most federal
! department sites are subdomains of gc.ca (e.g. cra-arc.gc.ca,
! statcan.gc.ca, ised-isde.gc.ca) -- confirm in practice that Brave's
! `site=` matches subdomains and not just the exact hostname, and adjust
! to explicit subdomains below if it doesn't.
$boost=6,site=canada.ca
$boost=6,site=gc.ca
$boost=5,site=parl.ca
$boost=5,site=bankofcanada.ca

! --- Add more entries below as you identify them -------------------------
